      - README.md, "How close", rewritten for its readers; the counts are
        still those of the runs of 2026-11-22 (no newer runs exist).  The
        1,543 rejected snippets named and split, from the stored
        samples.tsv of Proc-Spawner-results (2026-11-22-post-0.13): foreign
        1,458 = 389 only bash parses + 938 both parse, a feature dash lacks
        or runs otherwise (833 by the parser's detector, 105 by ShellCheck
        alone) + 125 neither + 6 only dash; subtle 40 = 26 listings + 7
        traces + 2 $PS1 + 1 x=$@ + 1 local x + 3 $- (open); the work list
        45.  Corrected: README said all 45 of the work list are forms both
        shells run alike, 44 of them for the parser to learn; section 4 of
        large-subset-state.md says 12 fail alike at run time, 11 stay
        rejected by decisions (B3, set, B1, D1), 3 are bash's arrays, and 19
