      - X84 fixed in the runner, decided 2026-11-23 (D6):
        large-subset-runcompare.pl -calls FILE (large-subset-provenance.tsv)
        takes the programs each snippet calls from the classifier's column
        CALLS (large-subset-blocks.pl -e), and a setup's standin; each one
        not on the list and no builtin of dash, bash or ShellSpawn (time,
        a keyword, gets one) gets a stand-in for that snippet's runs alone,
        made before and removed after them, seen through an overlay in the
        run's own mount namespace (with -env cowroot: in its own root), so
        that PATH and the other workers' runs stay as they were; the run
        record names them (standin_added), OUTDIR/calls.txt the file.
        doc/corpus.mk passes -calls in corpus-step3, corpus-step3-class,
        corpus-races, and in corpus-env-variants for fail, output, mtime
