      - pspawn-shell-windows.md, (s1): both test runners stop a file at 20
        MB; under Wine the same limit stops a Windows program (Git's yes
        writing into a file: 20,000,000 bytes, 0.17 s, status 153), but a
        pipe of Git's programs passed 15.6 to 17.1 MB in 5 seconds (three
        runs, Wine 9.0, PortableGit 2.47.1, 2026-11-22), so those snippets
        run out of time first.  It said that only the Linux runner limits
        the size of a file.
      - X82 (the measurement tools; fixed): taking dash's and bash's
        prefix off the messages, large-subset-runreport.pl's pattern
        (?:\S*\/)?dash: \d+:  (anywhere in a line) also took the word
        glued before the shell's path, as in "not found/usr/bin/dash: 1: ";
        the same pattern in large-subset-matchreport.pl,
        large-subset-builtins.pl and large-subset-repeat.pl.  Now the path
        begins with "/".  Made again from the runs of 2026-11-17 (no run
        made again): the base run's classes, 6 tldr snippets from messages
        as neither to messages as dash (23,287 and 72 became 23,293 and
