      - Where the C library's posix_spawn lacks closefrom alone (glibc
        before 2.34, musl), a call that asks for it no longer has its fd
        actions done in Perl's own process (TODO B, the next cycle's item
        1): closefrom N becomes a close of each fd from N up that the
        child has at that point (this process's fds without
        close-on-exec, and the targets of the call's earlier dup2 and
        open, less what it closed: closefrom_as_closes), and posix_spawn
        does them all in the child.  Not on Windows.  Unlike the
        library's closefrom it misses an fd that another thread opens
        meanwhile.  The fds without close-on-exec are read from
        /proc/self/fd where it is there (inheritable_from), not found by
        one fcntl for each number up to the limit on open files; system1
        (run_redirs) and the emulation (emulate_actions) use the same
        list.  Measured, with closefrom taken as missing and a limit of
        20,000 open files: a spawn with closefrom 3, 5.7 ms before, 1.3 ms
        now (1.3 to 1.6 ms with the library's own closefrom); through
        Run, 6.8 ms before, 2.4 ms now.
        Tests: t/spawner.t, 8 more (the call leaves everything to
        posix_spawn; an fd inherited from this process is closed; the
        list of closes; with dup2 missing too, done in this process as
        before); t/spawner.t passes as built, with closefrom missing,
