          From the run of 2026-11-16 to the first run of 2026-11-17 (IN1)
          The run of 2026-11-16 had the same code, but the recorders did not
          read their input. 27 samples changed class, none by a difference of
          ShellSpawn. We traced them sample by sample: the same run's records
          were also reported with the input's size and SHA-256 taken out of
          every log (the recorders still reading), and the 147 samples where a
          logged program read some input ran again with the recorder of
          2026-11-16 and with the new one.
          - **7 by what the programs are fed, which is now compared:**
            - `echo -e …` into a program (5: `| tsort`, `| nc host 80`, `|
              sudo tee -a …` twice, `| grep -v … | tail -1`), where dash's
              `echo` prints `-e` and interprets the backslashes, bash's and
              ShellSpawn's do not (from same to ShellSpawn as bash, as `echo
              -e` alone does);
            - `bind -P | grep … | perl …`: only bash has `bind`, so only bash
              feeds `perl` something (from messages only to ShellSpawn as
              dash, B2);
            - `v=5 env | less` (from same to ShellSpawn as neither): bash adds
              `SHLVL` and `_`, and the order of the variables differs, as for
              `env` alone (code `listing`). We compared the lists: dash's and
              ShellSpawn's hold the same variables.
          - **1 by the reading itself:** `md5sum * | sed -e '…/e'`, whose `e`
            command runs `mv` through `sh`. `mv`'s recorder reads sed's own
            input, a race with sed (from same to ShellSpawn as bash; with the
            recorder of 2026-11-16 the same in 5 runs of 5; named chance in
            `tools/large-subset-match-known.tsv`).
          - **The other 19 by timing,** as between earlier runs:
            - the messages of pipeline elements that mix otherwise (14: the
              tldr alternatives `a|b|c` 10, in both directions; `find … |
              xargs ls -lrt | awk …`, `find … | xargs ls -ld | more` and `sed
              … index.html | tee index.html`, from messages as neither to the
              same; `echo "fifo forever" | cat - fifo | tee fifo`, from
              messages as bash to as dash);
            - the races `ls -a | tee output.file` (from ShellSpawn differs to
              ShellSpawn as dash), `{ echo foo; cat bar; } | tee bar` and two
              `head` reading one pipe (from ShellSpawn as dash to as bash);
            - the `zenity` subshell (bash came out otherwise in the first run
              of 2026-11-17, so ShellSpawn as bash);
            - `ls -lR / | tee output.file`, which ended in dash too in the
              first run of 2026-11-17 (from timeout to ShellSpawn as neither);
            - 14+3+1+1=19.
          Beyond the classes, the reading changed, in those 147 samples:
          - the calls of one sample, `grep -L -r … | while read f; do mv "$f"
            out; done`, in all three alike: 10 calls before, 2 in the first
            run of 2026-11-17, because the first `mv`'s recorder reads the
            rest of the loop's input, so the loop ends;
          - the messages of 5: `xargs: …: terminated by signal 13` no more, as
